@Robert-Z9 — the walkthrough above covers it, so I won't repeat it. Two things to add:

- **I can run it for you.** Say "@claude do option A" (or B) and I'll push it to `epp_minor20260820` — once @krzysztofstaszalek confirms they're clear of the branch.
- **A revert is a one-time undo, not a permanent opt-out.** The wording the bot changed still trips the same Vale/Dale rules, so the next push that touches those five files will surface the same 28 fixes again. If a particular fix is wrong rather than merely unwanted (say, an acronym expansion that reads badly in EPP docs), the durable fix is adjusting the rule in `.claude/skills/dale/rules/` — happy to open a separate PR for that if you point at which ones.

